# Line endings are pinned rather than left to a clone's `core.autocrlf`.
#
# Two concrete reasons:
#
#  1. `pint --test` (in CI) enforces LF. A Windows checkout with
#     core.autocrlf=true materialises every file as CRLF, so pint failed on nearly
#     every PHP file locally while CI, on Linux, saw LF and failed on three --
#     a local check that disagrees with CI gets ignored.
#  2. `scripts/vendor.mjs` copies the working-tree bytes into the flow-node
#     marketplace's `_connector/` and `--check` compares them byte-for-byte.
#     Generated from a CRLF checkout, the copy differs from one generated on
#     Linux with no source change at all.
* text=auto eol=lf
